I don't like it; you can take that as forbidden or not as you like.

> Let's see.. let's look at an example of something by some guy
> named "Robin Powell":  I see "ralcinfra" used several times in
> "nicte cadzu" with no listing in jbovlaste, no explanation of what
> the word means, no place structure definition, no indication that
> it's a nonce term.  ditto "bavlamji", "tacsa'e" (which I assume is
> a typo for "tacysa'e"), etc. etc.  Need I go on????

Every lujvo I created in LNC has a complete definition.  I haven't
posted them all, and that's my bad, but they exist.  As an example,
here's a transcription of ralcinfra's definition:

    f1=c1 has an orgasm in response to stimulus f3 under conditions
    f4, thereby exhibiting sexuality/gender/sexual orientation c3
    (ka) by standard c4).  f2, c2 and all places of ralju subsumed
    by the concept of orgasm.

My *point* is that if you don't define the other places, you should
be using a tanru, because otherwise you lead readers to believe that
the word is important enough to warrant the 30+ minute process
involved in good lujvo creation.

> I didn't need to specify more than the x1 place, because that's
> all I used.

Then you should have used a tanru.  IME, YMMV.

